  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Death Don't Have No Mercy** (1 review): Reviewer's long-time favorite, first heard via Hot Tuna; this version is emotionally layered and builds up into the night sky [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Hey Jude**: rare: 13 archived performances [4]\n- **Spanish Jam**: rare: 8 archived performances [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **dco2023-05-23** (recommended): source not stated; 21 songs; 189 min; rated 5/5 by 2 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer says Jeff's keyboard playing comes alive and acts as a true counterpart to John's guitar [2]\n- Daytime heat peaked around 100-104 degrees, with the stage reportedly above 90 when the band started [3]\n- Parking lot was quaint and fun; fans sought shade, and most arrived close to showtime on a Tuesday [3]\n- Crowd was mild with no drama, though some attendees seemed to come just to hang out [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **dco2023-05-23**: taped by jbanyai97; transferred by jbanyai97; source: AKG ck8|a60m|c460b > Tascam DR-70D (24bit/44.1khz) [1]. Also: Shotgun mics in PAS configuration, 25cm spacing at 60 degrees, taped from the lawn about 50 feet from the stage, stand at 8 feet [1]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Fan art by Arizona Republic: [Dead and Company tour 2023: The farewell concert in Phoenix](https://www.azcentral.com/picture-gallery/entertainment/music/2023/05/24/dead-and-company-final-tour-phoenix-photos-2023/11939996002/) [5]",
